Launch & Connect to EC2

Launch an Amazon Linux 2 or Amazon Linux 2023 EC2 instance (t3.medium or bigger recommended).

Connect via SSH:

ssh -i your-key.pem ec2-user@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>

Update & Install Basics
sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv git

Create Project & Virtual Environment
mkdir ~/langchain_mistral_demo && cd ~/langchain_mistral_demo
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

Create requirements.txt
vi requirements.txt


Paste this inside:

requests
langchain
langchain-core
langchain-community
langchain-mistralai
langchain-text-splitters
langchain-openai
chromadb
sentence-transformers
python-dotenv


Save and exit (:wq).

 Install All Dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install requests
pip install requests mistralai langchain langchain-community faiss-cpu pyyaml
pip install -r requirements.txt

Set Mistral API Key

Replace with your real key:

echo 'export MISTRAL_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc


Verify:

echo $MISTRAL_API_KEY

 Copy Your Script to EC2

Create the script file:

vi mistral_raw_api.py
vi demo_langchain_mistral.py
vi compare_mistral_vs_langchain.py



Make it executable (optional):

chmod +x (all files individually)

 Run the Demo
python3 mistral_raw_api.py
python3 demo_langchain_mistral.py
python3 compare_mistral_vs_langchain.py


Give some random prompts and test it for different scripts and check the difference
